{"agent_id":"pp3g-hngZ-audit-phase-2-post-hoc-read-only-flag-only-8bbb","agent_seq":2,"timestamp":"2026-08-18T06:58:30.357963745Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"ee215a83-53ea-467e-8252-47f6367286c8","comment_uuid":"1aa8dd9e-ea04-4689-b878-b77125da5152","author":"pp3g-hngZ-audit-phase-2-post-hoc-read-only-flag-only-8bbb","content":"# AUDIT RESULT — Independent Verification of Hook Research (#388, #389)\n\n## Audit Verdict: CONDITIONAL PASS\n\n### Preconditions (must be met before implementation)\n1. The doc-check-guard design must be validated with a live smoke test before merging\n2. The \"doc-read confirmation\" mechanism must be chosen and its reliability assessed (comment-kind is recommended but untested)\n3. The interaction between doc-check-guard and existing guards (crosslink-guard, rtk-guard) must be tested for ordering hazards\n4. The human-terminal interception gap must be explicitly acknowledged as a known limitation in any shipped design\n\n---\n\n## 1. Architectural Assessment\n\n### [OK] — tool.execute.before CAN fire before 'crosslink kickoff run' / 'crosslink swarm launch'\n**Evidence**: fork/opencode-src/packages/opencode/src/session/tools.ts:106-107 — every tool execution (including bash) triggers plugin hook via `plugin.trigger(\"tool.execute.before\", { tool: item.id, sessionID, callID }, { args })`. Since 'crosslink kickoff run' and 'crosslink swarm launch' are Bash tool calls (not slash commands), this hook fires before execution. The existing crosslink-guard.ts:967-972 already intercepts bash via this exact mechanism (toolLower === 'bash' branch).\n**Verification**: grep for 'tool.execute.before' in tools.ts confirmed at lines 106, 175, 258, 338, 402 — covers all tool types including bash.\n\n### [OK] — command.execute.before does NOT fire for crosslink CLI commands\n**Evidence**: fork/opencode-src/packages/opencode/src/session/prompt.ts:1464-1468 — `command.execute.before` is triggered in the Command context with `{ command: input.command, sessionID, arguments }`. This is the slash-command path only. Bash tool calls go through tools.ts, not prompt.ts's Command handler.\n**Verification**: confirmed no overlap between the two trigger sites.\n\n### [OK] — write/edit filePath matching can gate hook-config.json edits\n**Evidence**: crosslink-guard.ts:990-996 — the plugin checks `output.args?.filePath` for write/edit tools (the ~/.claude/ exemption at line 991). The same pattern can check for .crosslink/hook-config.json. orchestrator-guard.ts:81-103 demonstrates blocking by tool name for write/edit/MCP tools.\n**Verification**: crosslink-guard.ts:991 reads `output.args?.filePath as string` — this is the exact field a doc-check guard would match against.\n\n### [OK] — throw -> tool-error propagation mechanism confirmed\n**Evidence**: fork/opencode-src/packages/opencode/src/plugin/index.ts:292 — `yield* Effect.promise(async () => fn(input, output))`. When a hook throws, Effect.promise converts the rejection to Effect.fail, which propagates up. fork/opencode-src/packages/opencode/src/session/llm/ai-sdk.ts:249-262 — the AI SDK's tool-error event is surfaced to the model as the tool result.\n**Verification**: The chain is: hook throw -> Effect.promise rejection -> Effect.fail -> tool-error -> model sees error message. This is exactly how crosslink-guard's MANDATORY COMPLIANCE blocks work (crosslink-guard.ts:984,1011,1057,1129,1207).\n\n### [OK] — rtk-guard proves command mutation is viable\n**Evidence**: rtk-guard.ts:406 — `(output as { args: { command: string } }).args.command = rewritten`. This mutates the bash command before execution. A doc-check guard could use the same pattern to prepend 'cat .crosslink/knowledge/<page> && ' to the command.\n**Verification**: rtk-guard.ts demonstrates the full mutation pattern including loop guard (lines 316-325), opt-out (lines 328-337), and structural safety checks.\n\n### [OK] — permission.ask is confirmed dead\n**Evidence**: fork/opencode-src/packages/plugin/src/index.ts:261 — declared in Hooks type. grep for 'trigger.*permission.ask' across the entire fork/opencode-src/packages/opencode/src directory returned zero matches. The plugin.trigger() calls in plugin/index.ts:282-295 iterate registered hooks by name, but no code path calls trigger(\"permission.ask\", ...).\n**Verification**: 30 plugin.trigger() call sites found; none target permission.ask.\n\n### [CONCERN] — experimental.* hooks are version-pinned and unstable\n**Evidence**: fork/opencode-src/packages/plugin/src/index.ts:282-330 — the experimental hooks (chat.messages.transform, chat.system.transform, session.compacting, etc.) are prefixed with 'experimental.' by contract. Their signatures could change between versions.\n**Impact**: A doc-check guard relying on experimental.chat.system.transform for persistent system-prompt injection would break on upstream changes. Recommendation: use tool.execute.before throw (proven, stable) as the primary gate, not experimental hooks.\n\n### [CONCERN] — Hook ordering is observed, not guaranteed\n**Evidence**: opencode.json:4-8 lists plugins in explicit order: orchestrator-guard, crosslink-guard, rtk-guard. fork/opencode-src/packages/opencode/src/config/plugin.ts (referenced by research) shows plugins are loaded from both explicit config and directory scan, with dedup on file URL. The observed order is alphabetical within directory scan, but this is not API-guaranteed.\n**Impact**: A new doc-check-guard.ts must tolerate running before or after crosslink-guard.ts. If it runs after crosslink-guard allows a 'crosslink *' command (via allowed_bash_prefixes), the doc-check can still intercept. If it runs before, it can gate before crosslink-guard sees the command. Both orderings work for the doc-check use case.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Process Assessment\n\n### [OK] — Research agents (#388, #389) followed the read-only protocol\n**Evidence**: Both issues show plan comments, progress checkpoints, and result comments. No file modifications were made. Both agents correctly identified as read-only research tasks.\n\n### [OK] — Research findings are largely accurate and well-sourced\n**Evidence**: I independently verified:\n- Hook event enumeration matches the Hooks interface at fork/opencode-src/packages/plugin/src/index.ts:222-335\n- tool.execute.before trigger sites confirmed in tools.ts (lines 106, 175, 258, 338, 402)\n- command.execute.before is slash-command-only (prompt.ts:1464)\n- Worktree hooks limited to crosslink_config.py + heartbeat.py (.claude/hooks/ directory inspection)\n- throw -> tool-error chain confirmed (plugin/index.ts:292, ai-sdk.ts:249)\n- permission.ask dead (zero trigger call sites)\n\n### [CONCERN] — Research #389 claims 'experimental.chat.system.transform pushes to append' but this is imprecise\n**Evidence**: fork/opencode-src/packages/plugin/src/index.ts:291-296 defines the output as `{ system: string[] }`. The agent.ts:381 trigger site shows `{ system }` where system is initialized as `[PROMPT_GENERATE]`. A plugin pushing to output.system would append to this array. The research's language 'pushes to append' is directionally correct but the mechanism is array mutation, not a dedicated push API.\n**Impact**: Low — the array mutation works as described, but implementers should know the system prompt is rebuilt per-request (agent.ts:380), so pushes are ephemeral, not persistent across turns.\n\n### [CONCERN] — Research #389 overstates the 'comment-kind discipline' recommendation\n**Evidence**: The issueHasCommentKind function (crosslink-guard.ts:665-687) queries .crosslink/issues.db via bun:sqlite. This works for crosslink-tracked issues but requires: (a) the .crosslink/issues.db to exist and be populated, (b) the agent to have posted a comment with the right kind before the gated action. The research recommends this as 'the most consistent with existing repo discipline' but it's untested for the doc-check use case.\n**Impact**: Medium — if the issues.db is stale or the comment hasn't synced, the gate could falsely pass or falsely block. A simpler mechanism (sentinel file or per-session in-memory tracking) might be more reliable for an initial implementation.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Systemic Risks Identified\n\n### Risk: Human-terminal interception gap\n**Impact**: A human running 'crosslink kickoff run' in a terminal is not intercepted by any plugin hook. Only agent sessions (via OpenCode or Claude Code) are gated.\n**Mitigation**: This is an accepted limitation. The doc-check hook is designed for agent sessions, not human terminal usage. Document this explicitly in the design doc.\n\n### Risk: Cross-session agent identity clobbering\n**Impact**: If doc-read state is stored per-process (not per-sessionID), a reviewer subagent's reads could satisfy the parent orchestrator's gate.\n**Mitigation**: Key doc-read state by sessionID, following the pattern established in crosslink-guard.ts:809-812 (runtimeAgentBySession Map keyed by sessionID) after the #204 regression.\n\n### Risk: MCP tool args shape differs from native tools\n**Impact**: filesystem_write_file / filesystem_edit_file carry 'path' not 'filePath'. A doc-check guard matching filePath would miss MCP file writes.\n**Mitiation**: Handle both shapes, following orchestrator-guard.ts:33-39 which matches by tool name for MCP tools.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Recommendations\n\n### Recommendation: Where the doc-check hook should live\n**New file**: .opencode/plugins/doc-check-guard.ts (auto-discovered via Glob.scan; add to opencode.json for ordering control)\n**Hook**: tool.execute.before (bash + write/edit)\n**Config**: Extend .crosslink/hook-config.json with a 'doc_check' block\n**Primary mechanism**: throw Error with instructive message (proven by crosslink-guard)\n**Fallback mechanism**: command mutation to prepend doc-read (proven by rtk-guard)\n**Priority**: High\n\n### Recommendation: doc-read confirmation mechanism\n**Preferred**: Per-session in-memory tracking of 'read' tool calls for required pages (cheap, no external dependencies, matches guard pattern)\n**Alternative**: Comment-kind discipline via issues.db (durable audit trail but untested for this use case)\n**Avoid**: Sentinel files (requires file system mutation, conflicts with read-only agent role)\n**Priority**: High\n\n### Recommendation: Implementation order\n1. Prototype doc-check-guard.ts with throw-only blocking (no mutation)\n2. Smoke test with a real kickoff/swarm dispatch\n3. Add command-mutation variant if throw-only proves insufficient\n4. Test ordering interaction with crosslink-guard and rtk-guard\n5. Document human-terminal gap as known limitation\n**Priority**: High\n\n---\n\n## 5. Files Verified (with line references)\n\n| File | Lines | Claim Verified |\n|------|-------|---------------|\n| .crosslink/hook-config.json | 1-237 | Config structure, agent_overrides.by_type, allowed_bash_prefixes |\n| .claude/settings.json | 1-75 | PreToolUse/PostToolUse/SessionStart/UserPromptSubmit hook registration |\n| .claude/hooks/ | directory | Only crosslink_config.py + heartbeat.py in worktree (confirmed) |\n| .opencode/opencode.json | 1-46 | Plugin array: orchestrator-guard, crosslink-guard, rtk-guard |\n| .opencode/plugins/crosslink-guard.ts | 1-1220 | tool.execute.before intercept, throw blocking, issueHasCommentKind |\n| .opencode/plugins/rtk-guard.ts | 1-415 | tool.execute.before command mutation, V1_VALIDATED allowlist |\n| .opencode/plugins/orchestrator-guard.ts | 1-108 | tool.execute.before write blocking by agent type |\n| fork/opencode-src/packages/plugin/src/index.ts | 222-335 | Full Hooks interface, permission.ask declared |\n| fork/opencode-src/packages/opencode/src/session/tools.ts | 106-107 | tool.execute.before trigger for all tools |\n| fork/opencode-src/packages/opencode/src/session/prompt.ts | 1464-1468 | command.execute.before trigger (slash commands only) |\n| fork/opencode-src/packages/opencode/src/plugin/index.ts | 282-295 | trigger implementation: Effect.promise async wrapper |\n| fork/opencode-src/packages/opencode/src/session/llm/ai-sdk.ts | 249-262 | tool-error propagation to model |\n| fork/opencode-src/packages/opencode/src/agent/agent.ts | 380-381 | experimental.chat.system.transform trigger site |","created_at":"2026-08-18T06:58:30.348241439Z","kind":"note","signed_by":"SHA256:owyll8ElWkthckS6AX1pLAgX73hKY2i2e7lEyAFCcmw","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgbCq4SAiBmQFq+Agg8ANNTTnt0jq1qLDvYXUsc5sZJucAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA0LgCB7FPAPcLig91aMNZAVT3QeKqH2e0wdm5zH7z+IXfXwXF/IR+WmY49TaevNYStGppjJoDwyBbTcot2VGgCA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:owyll8ElWkthckS6AX1pLAgX73hKY2i2e7lEyAFCcmw","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgbCq4SAiBmQFq+Agg8ANNTTnt0jq1qLDvYXUsc5sZJucAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMNwGJeck9ceQRn3UykGmg6F3IOzYk3GplcIp8hreyg3kgAdgk+lgzVIrDZBGxc+aQ6ZjRkvqm6gcNu/hT1HCg0="}
